From 09100e8c069061242d4773839df765014994e704 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bcup02 <55205420+bcup02@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 13:27:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(projection): receiver config errors are retryable, not
 terminal REJECTED (v0.13.2) (#7)

deliver_projection_v2 mapped every receiver ok:false response to a terminal
REJECTED. A REJECTED dispatch is filtered out of outstanding_projection_intents
forever, and enqueue_projection_intent dedupes by intent key, so a burned
intent cannot be re-queued from the ledger.

momentum's first v2-delivery run hit this: the shared Apps Script Web App was
an old version that routes a v2 payload to the legacy SHARED_SECRET check ->
{ok:false, error:"unauthorized"}. The drain marked all 26 backlog intents
terminal REJECTED in one pass.

- Only a structurally-invalid payload is terminal now: provenance_invalid /
  open_projection_invalid / close_projection_invalid. Every other receiver
  error (unauthorized, signature_invalid, source_not_allowed,
  unsupported_action from a stale deployment, request_not_fresh,
  sheet_not_found, malformed_request, ...) is a config/deploy problem the
  SAME intent survives once fixed -> TRANSPORT_FAILED, so the durable outbox
  keeps it.
- tests: existing terminal test now uses provenance_invalid; new
  test_receiver_config_errors_stay_retryable_so_the_intent_is_not_burned
  parametrizes 6 config errors. test_projection_outbox's mock-submit example
  error updated for consistency. 112 -> 113.
- version 0.13.1 -> 0.13.2; consumer-release-runbook entry.

Co-authored-by: bcup02 <columnbb@gmail.com>
Co-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
